====================================================================================
Multi-bit grid for GLOBAL search: does the coarse grid miss the wide-R best?
====================================================================================
  Heisenberg N=4, block of 4 params, 3 centres

        R   b  levels   points    best E  gap to b=3  minima
  ----------------------------------------------------------
    0.600   1       2       16   -3.6502                 1.3
    0.600   2       4      256   -3.7832                 1.7
    0.600   3       8     4096   -3.7940                 1.3
                                              b=1 worse than b=3 by 0.1438

    1.200   1       2       16   -3.0711                 1.7
    1.200   2       4      256   -4.1342                 1.7
    1.200   3       8     4096   -4.2423                 2.0
                                              b=1 worse than b=3 by 1.1713

    1.571   1       2       16   -2.3099                 1.7
    1.571   2       4      256   -4.0027                 3.7
    1.571   3       8     4096   -4.3121                 3.3
                                              b=1 worse than b=3 by 2.0022

  If the b=1 gap is ~0, the two-level corners already reach whatever the
  finer grid reaches, and extra bits buy no global-search power - the
  coarse-to-fine cascade then reduces to the R decay schedule that
  _execute_walk already runs.
